WEBVTT

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:10.170
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:20.040
Rental Magica

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:28.020
The shadow of the moon as it waxes and wanes...
Michikakeru tsuki no kage sotto

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:37.700
...gently stirs the beat of sorrow in your heart.
kanashimi no kodou furuwasu

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:42.390
Its wandering attraction...
Samayou inryoku

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:47.330
...reflected in your eyes.
hitomi ni utsushite

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:53.310
You will surpass the darkness of Ioneliness.
Kodoku no yami wo koeteyuku

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:59.010
You know that truth in your heart.
Shinjitsu wa kono mune ni

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:04.690
That gentleness will become your strength.
Yasashisa wa tsuyosa ni naru

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:09.330
Don't be afraid. Believe.
Osorenaide shinjiru koto

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:14.170
The brilliance that blooms in the cosmos eternally...
Sora ni saku kirameki wa towa ni

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.140
...embraces the voice of time.
toki no koe dakishime

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:24.210
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.940
Let me hear.
Kikasete

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:33.680
Wind, speak to me.
Kaze tsutaete

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:40.190
Tell me what courage is.
Yuuki wo

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.600
Due to an accident with a large trailer truck,

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.340
all service on the Gulf westbound line and the...

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:54.040
...Ariake local trains past
Ooi has been suspended.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:56.870
Nekoyashiki!

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.510
We'll reach you momentarily, Mr. President.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.580
I thought you said this thing was a dog!

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.750
It's a mammal with sharp teeth
that walks on four legs and barks,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.520
so what else would you call it but a dog?

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.820
But, just look at it!

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.050
I don't think I can handle this.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.040
You're sure this is going to work, right?

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.070
It won't catch up to us, will it?

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:29.880
Sorry, Mr. President.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:35.580
We've had to cut expenses, so the truck
we're in was the cheapest I could rent.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:36.450
Hey! Stop that!

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.720
Hey! Stop that!
But the plan should be foolproof. Don't worry.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.650
But the plan should be foolproof. Don't worry.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.320
It's the "should be" part that worries me.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.920
We're almost to the junction.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.690
Be ready on your end, Mr. President.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:48.820
R-Right.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.040
Mikan, if you'd be so kind.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:54.800
Gotcha!

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.440
Tohokami, Emitame,

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:59.010
Kan Gon Shin Son Ri Kon Da Ken!

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.940
Remove what is unclean, and purify!

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.310
Its spell power is stronger than I thought!

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.580
It might be more accurate to say
"malice" rather than "spell power."

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.190
Perhaps resentment for the
one who ran its owner down...

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.410
Now, Mr. President!

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.750
Accept your fate!

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.820
There's nowhere left for you to run!

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:13.850
Hold it!

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.520
You won't escape!

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:32.330
I have to do this, if only so that
the boss's efforts aren't wasted!

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:37.340
What the?!

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.380
Uh! Look! I've got talismans here, see?

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.580
Brother Pres' barrier is so weak!

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.150
Worse than that,

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:54.050
it seems the dog has figured out
which of us is the weakest.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.590
What are you doing to our president?!

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.960
It's trying to break through.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.910
Boss! It's useless! Let go!

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.710
Oh, no! Empty! I overexerted myself!

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.590
If I let go, it'll mean trouble for
the company and everyone else!

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:33.290
But I'm nearly at the end of my rope here...

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.260
Boss! Don't waste your strength!

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.160
No good! I can't aim with him in the way.

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:51.800
Honami, out of the way!

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.140
Adelicia?

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.340
Oh, great. Enter the big boss.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.310
Wow, cool!

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.990
Why? Is Goetia bidding on
this job along with us?

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:09.460
Obey me!

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.930
Behold the seal of Solomon I carry!

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:17.870
In the name of the Lord, thou shalt obey my will!

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:22.530
Come forth, Forneus!
The marquis who rules 29 legions!

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.290
No mercy, as usual from you.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:45.720
That's not like you, Honami.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:49.630
Hesitating like that in order to protect
this cowardly boss of yours.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.570
Coward or not, he's still our company president!

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:58.110
Considering Astral isn't very
powerful at the best of times,

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:01.910
do you think half-assed performances
like that will let you beat Goetia?

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.050
Forneus!

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.000
I wonder how she found out we were here.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.130
"The most direct path to a monster
is the one it blazes itself."

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.500
That's common sense in
England and China, too.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:27.470
My rough guess is that she followed us.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:31.230
Itsuki?

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.490
Say, Kuroha?

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:47.420
Yes?

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.490
The dog... It's not lonely anymore, is it?

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.630
No, I'd say it isn't.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:57.900
Itsuki?

00:07:58.640 --> 00:07:59.370
Icchan!

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:18.450
Just normal backlash? He's too defenseless.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:30.430
The world is more full of magic
than most people think.

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:35.040
Mage Recruiting Agency
ASTRAL
We rent mages to meet your demands.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:50.310
Do you have some business with Astral?

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.470
Boss, if you had just let go
and gotten out of the way,

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:06.530
I could've taken it out before
Addie jumped in on the action.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:08.630
Sorry.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:13.880
Brother Pres was riding
the bike in my place! Right?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.080
Um, well! I just thought it would
be too much for a girl to do, so...

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:22.020
Even so, considering the cost of
the truck rental, Mikan's tamagushi,

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.850
and the charms for sealing
that dog spirit, it comes to...

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:28.460
And just where are we going to get the
money to pay these expenses, Boss?!

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:30.670
Um, well...

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:31.530
Excuse me.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:33.820
We have a customer.

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:37.230
Miss Kunugi?

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.170
Oh, is this a friend of yours, Mr. President?

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.770
She's a classmate of mine from school.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:46.910
Now that you mention it,
she's wearing the same uniform as Honami.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.620
Iba, you're the president of this company?

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:53.520
In name only, as you can see.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.990
Though, I wish you would
take the job more seriously.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:00.760
I didn't know Honami worked here, too.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.890
Yeah, although Honami's
an expert in Celtic magic.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:08.930
Mikan and Nekoyashiki are
experts in Shinto magic.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:10.940
Strictly speaking,

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:14.640
I specialize in using Onmyoudou to control
guardian spirits called shikigami,

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.670
particularly cats.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.640
I think cats are adorable.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:19.680
Truly the greatest treasures of the world-

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.550
And finally, our apprentice, Miss Kuroha.
Truly the greatest treasures of the world-

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.820
Anyway, what do you want
with Astral, Miss Kunugi?

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.350
MAGES FOR HIRE!

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:33.220
Here.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:36.160
My father's.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:37.700
Mage Recruiting Agency Astral

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:41.600
Where did you get such an old business card?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.340
I think it may have been my grandfather's.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.010
May have been?

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.140
There's no way for me to confirm that.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.440
What do you mean?

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:53.050
He vanished. Like he was spirited away.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.240
Spirited away?

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.620
That's why I want you to look for him!

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:03.290
Please allow me to rent the
services of the mages of Astral.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.760
What sort of person is Miss Kunugi?

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:12.960
I'm not one to talk, but she doesn't
really stand out in any way.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.640
Well actually, she's our class president,

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:19.210
though I get the feeling she wasn't
elected for being popular,

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:22.570
but rather because she's a diligent worker
people can push off annoying tasks on.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.880
It's not so much that she's really amiable.

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:31.180
She seems more the type who avoids
rejection by not getting close to people.

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:38.420
Right on time.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:39.990
Another job?

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:42.690
Because Honami is such an expert mage,

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.830
she's constantly getting called out for stuff.

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:46.630
An expert mage...

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:49.430
It seems so absurd.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:54.640
Before my grandfather vanished,
I might not have believed it.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:58.240
This is his room.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:02.140
This house seems so warm.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:04.310
Warm...

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:10.890
My parents were killed in
a landslide 5 years ago.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.390
Only my grandfather and I were saved.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:22.770
Ever since, my grandfather has
immersed himself in collecting antiques...

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:24.760
...like a man possessed.

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:27.570
What are you doing?

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:31.730
I thought I told you never to come into my room.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:35.340
Don't lay a finger on any of my belongings.

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:38.840
It got so that he lived only for his antiques.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:42.250
As though he was growing distant from me.

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:49.230
This house where just the two
of us lived is dark and cold.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:54.970
But when you called it a warm
house just now, I remembered.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:13:00.600
When I was little, my grandfather's
hands were warm when he held me.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:04.800
Could you tell us any details
about when he disappeared?

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:12.020
I came home from school that day...

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:30.040
I'm positive I heard it then. That laughter...

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:31.740
Laughter?

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:35.530
I haven't seen my grandfather since that day.

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.980
I went to the address on that business
card immediately to get help.

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.340
That's when I saw you there, Iba.

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:46.150
I went a few times, but never
had the courage to go in.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.490
You should have asked me about it at school.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:53.530
Iba, why did you become the president of Astral?

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:59.230
My dad was originally the president,
but he disappeared 7 years ago.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:04.400
So, I kinda got stuck being his successor.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:16.980
That's a spell purification design, isn't it?

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:20.590
It looks like it's derived from the
Shugendou school of mysticism.

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:26.280
Shouldn't you two be with the president?

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:27.960
Big Sister Honami?

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:29.690
Right.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:33.330
The president and Kuroha are in the
house right now talking to Miss Kunugi.

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:38.330
Never mind that. What are
you doing here, Honami?

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:42.540
I heard from The Association that a mage
who'd violated an anti-spirit taboo...

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:46.950
...had set up a studio at the foot of this
mountain and came to investigate it.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:52.680
It looks like the anti-spirit fetish was
discharged about 5 years ago.

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:56.880
Miss Kunugi lost her parents
in a landslide 5 years ago.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:58.520
Do you suppose?!

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:04.690
What's it all mean?

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:09.400
An anti-spirit taboo... In short,
a spell to resurrect the dead!

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:18.770
What if Miss Kunugi's grandfather
was mortally injured 5 years ago?

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.880
You mean, her grandfather
cast the taboo to survive?

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:24.690
As a result,

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:25.120
HAIL!
As a result,

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.780
he gradually lost the ability to control
the spell power, and it ran wild.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:47.470
Look... Look... Look...

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.180
I may not be able to keep this up!

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:53.880
Look! Look!

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:05.460
Iba!

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:08.120
No... Miss Kunugi!

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:10.090
No, don't!

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:22.170
Mikan, Nekoyashiki, Honami...

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:24.440
As your president, I order you!

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:35.410
Mikan, give me a misogi on its left-rear
flank from 15 to 45 degrees!

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:43.890
Nekoyashiki, right flank, 45 degrees,
10 meters out! A fire line charm!

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:50.430
Honami, left side, 60 degrees up!
Shoot a mistletoe arrow!

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.350
We did it! Huh?

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:17.890
Boss!

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.740
Please don't go!

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:33.110
Miss Kunugi...

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:39.480
I won't go...

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:40.740
Grandpa?

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:44.260
I swear... Grandpa...

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:46.230
...isn't going anywhere.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.920
We'll be together forever and ever.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.490
Grandpa...

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:56.260
I won't leave you alone, Shoko.

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:59.200
Miss Kunugi, no!

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:06.710
I made a promise to my grandpa...
I didn't want to be alone.

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:09.870
Kunugi, you aren't alone!

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:20.360
Isn't that so?

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:27.700
You both made that promise, so only
you can let your grandfather go.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.570
I'll help you, too!

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:40.010
Enough. I'm all right now.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:45.010
So, Grandpa, it's okay for you to go.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.910
Thank you, Grandpa.

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:54.220
The gentleness within you is what saved you.

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.500
Miss Kunugi?

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:14.410
I'm here!

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:20.450
Thank goodness.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:25.150
Boss!

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:30.320
Brother Pres, you're so reckless!

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:31.560
Are you all right?

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:36.530
You okay?

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:51.940
I'm sorry.

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:05.530
According to Honami,

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:12.300
your grandfather stuck these fetishes inside
the antiques to allow himself to stay alive.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:13.830
"Fetishes?"

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:15.210
In other words,

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:19.670
your grandfather endowed these pots
and wall scrolls with magical powers.

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:24.180
But since he had committed a taboo,
it warped the spell.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:28.080
So, to protect you from
spell wave contamination...

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.990
He kept me at a distance.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:36.020
A mage who commits a taboo will
be so consumed by the magic...

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:39.230
...that it will even change his personality.

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:43.740
That's why his desire to simply
not leave you all alone...

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:46.370
...warped him into what you saw.

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:50.330
But I...

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:54.750
I think that somewhere in your grandfather...

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:57.310
...were still feelings that
the magic hadn't violated.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:01.390
That's why, in the very end,
he sent you to Astral for help.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:10.360
Of course, the Astral your
grandfather had relied on...

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:12.390
...was the company under my father's leadership.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:15.300
When it happened, for just a moment,

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:18.140
I think I saw grandpa's kind smile.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:23.400
You were the one who brought
me back to this world, Iba.

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:26.740
That wasn't your father's power.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:31.680
Could I please have your business card, Iba?

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:48.430
Iba, thank you.

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:53.800
HOW
TO
MANAGE
A
COMPANY

00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:00.470
So, apparently you took on
another two-bit job, huh?

00:22:02.850 --> 00:22:05.510
True, we didn't make that much money off of it.

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:10.320
And just how long does the boss of
the world-famous Geotia company...

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:12.880
...plan on staying out here
in the remote Far East?

00:22:13.090 --> 00:22:16.630
And just how long do you plan
to stay with a half-assed...

00:22:16.630 --> 00:22:19.660
...mish-mash of a company like Astral?

00:22:20.170 --> 00:22:22.070
Only our president is half-assed!

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:25.040
Oh, is that so?

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:28.010
If you have no business here,
why don't you shove off back to England?

00:22:28.010 --> 00:22:30.040
Sure the real reason you want me gone...

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:32.050
...isn't to get the clients I'll leave behind?

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:35.170
Oh, like you have any other
reason for hanging around here?

00:22:36.220 --> 00:22:37.620
My eye...

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:38.450
Itsuki?
Boss?

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:39.910
Does your eye hurt?
Does your eye hurt?

00:22:41.690 --> 00:22:45.250
It's nothing. The spell power from
you two is just so strong, that, well...

00:22:45.860 --> 00:22:48.790
No matter what, I won't show any mercy to Astral.

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:51.630
Get ready, because we have a ton of
homework to do when we get back tonight.

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:15.480
The world is more full of
magic than most people think.

00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:42.540
Over and over, holding my wounded hand...
Kizutsuku te wo nandomo tsunaide

00:23:42.950 --> 00:23:50.950
...you walk this uncertain path with me...
fuan bakari no kono michi wo aruite

00:23:52.230 --> 00:24:04.000
...amidst the days as they slowly drift by.
yukkuri nagareta hibi no naka de bokura ga

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:15.920
The things we obtain are so warm, so beloved.
Te ni shita mono wa konna ni atatakute itoshinda

00:24:15.920 --> 00:24:22.190
Please, as time goes by, let's keep right on...
Nee konomama toki no naka

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:26.690
...laughing and walking together.
waratte aruite yukou

00:24:27.560 --> 00:24:30.960
It's because you're with me...
Kimi ga iru kara

00:24:30.960 --> 00:24:36.060
...that I can keep moving forward.
mae ni susumerunda

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:47.940
Now our feelings are becoming one...
Ima bokura no omoi ga hitotsu ni natte

00:24:48.320 --> 00:24:51.990
...and showing the path to us.
michi wo shimesunda

00:24:51.990 --> 00:24:56.220
So please, keep on holding my hand...
Dakara kono te zutto

00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:59.320
...and never let it go...
hanasanaide

00:25:00.790 --> 00:25:01.800
Magi Night [MADOU NO YORU]

00:25:01.800 --> 00:25:03.260
Magi Night [MADOU NO YORU]
Do you know what a Magi Night is?

00:25:03.260 --> 00:25:04.200
Magi Night [MADOU NO YORU]
Um... No. What is it?

00:25:04.200 --> 00:25:05.130
Um... No. What is it?

00:25:05.130 --> 00:25:09.300
A Magi Night is a night when the power
of magic and the occult run rampant.

00:25:09.300 --> 00:25:12.210
Yikes! I get scared just thinking about it!

00:25:12.210 --> 00:25:13.770
Is that all for today, Prof. Miwa?

